# XCU uux
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# uux runs a command on a remote system; remote execution cannot be
# observed, but the page requires four redirection operators to be refused
# before anything is queued, and that check needs no remote system.

assertion  XCU.uux.001
anchor     utilities/uux.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/uux.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       UU
since      1992
says       A command string using the redirection operators >>, <<, >| or >&
           is rejected with a non-zero exit status.
test       t/001-redirections-refused.sh

assertion  XCU.uux.002
anchor     utilities/uux.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/uux.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/uux.html#OPERANDS
class      untestable
since      1992
says       uux gathers the files named in the command string, runs the
           pipeline on the named system and sends its standard output to a
           file, with -j writing a job identification, -n suppressing mail
           and -p taking the command's standard input from uux's.
reason     Remote execution needs a configured remote system and a
           communications line, and the effects (a job queue entry, a run on
           another machine, mail) lie outside the test system.
